{"name":"Building Block","hex":"#afafa7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"building block","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A component that is part of a larger construction, such as a brick or a stone.\nA block made of wood or plastic that is used as a children's toy and can be stacked or joined to form a larger structure.","A block made of wood or plastic that is used as a children's toy and can be stacked or joined to form a larger structure."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/building_block"}],"entries":[{"title":"Building block (chemistry)","blocks":[{"text":"Building block is a term in chemistry which is used to describe a virtual molecular fragment or a real chemical compound the molecules of which possess reactive functional groups. Building blocks are used for bottom-up modular assembly of molecular architectures: nano-particles, metal-organic frameworks, organic molecular constructs, supra-molecular complexes. Using building blocks ensures strict control of what a final compound or a (supra)molecular construct will be."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Molecular_BB_House_157.jpg/330px-Molecular_BB_House_157.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Building_block_(chemistry)"},{"title":"Building blocks (toy)","blocks":[{"text":"Building blocks are modular construction parts, usually made of plastic, which can be assembled in a form-fit manner. The basic components are usually cuboid-shaped, cylindrically studded at the top in a grid pattern, hollow-bodied at the bottom and smooth at the sides. The structured upper surface interacts by friction and positive locking with the correspondingly negative lower surface of other clamping components, so that complex designs can be assembled. The design allows the parts to be connected with compressive force and the blocks to be clamped with plastic pins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Lego_by_Christian_Ursilva_%282025%29.jpg/330px-Lego_by_Christian_Ursilva_%282025%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Building_blocks_(toy)"},{"title":"Building","blocks":[{"text":"A building or edifice is an enclosed structure with a roof, walls and often windows, usually standing permanently in one place, such as a house or factory. Buildings come in a variety of sizes, shapes, and functions, and have been adapted throughout history in response to numerous factors, from available building materials to weather conditions, land prices, ground conditions, specific uses, prestige, and aesthetic reasons. To better understand the concept, see Nonbuilding structure for contrast."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Philae_temple_at_night.jpg/330px-Philae_temple_at_night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Building"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/SaxagliptinBB.jpg/500px-SaxagliptinBB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/SaxagliptinBB.jpg/500px-SaxagliptinBB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An anti-diabetic drug Saxagliptin and two building blocks BB1 and BB2 from which it could be synthesized","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaxagliptinBB.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Lego_evolution.jpg/500px-Lego_evolution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Lego_evolution.jpg/1280px-Lego_evolution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Lego_evolution.jpg/500px-Lego_evolution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kiddicraft and Lego building blocks in different colors","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALego_evolution.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/LegoSpritzgussDetail.JPG/500px-LegoSpritzgussDetail.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/LegoSpritzgussDetail.JPG/1280px-LegoSpritzgussDetail.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/LegoSpritzgussDetail.JPG/500px-LegoSpritzgussDetail.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Injection mold for 4×2 Lego blocks","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALegoSpritzgussDetail.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/LegoSpritzgussDetail1.JPG/500px-LegoSpritzgussDetail1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/LegoSpritzgussDetail1.JPG/1280px-LegoSpritzgussDetail1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/LegoSpritzgussDetail1.JPG/500px-LegoSpritzgussDetail1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Injection mold top","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALegoSpritzgussDetail1.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Lego-all-combinations-of-two_bricks.jpg/500px-Lego-all-combinations-of-two_bricks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Lego-all-combinations-of-two_bricks.jpg/500px-Le